  "text_md": "# Display Font (Font Type=3):\n\n![](<44154425b027bf4ad655b4ffa70d8f914485ab1f9173c2e9f693b795cde08df9_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\nDisplay\n\nPFD Definition Font\n\nFont\n\nnumber\n\nCode page\n\nand font\n\nFont\n\ntype\n\ncharacter\n\nset\n\n3\n\nT1D0BASE\n\nCode\n\npage\n\nFont character\n\n. set\n\nC0D0DB10\n\nPoint\n\nsize\n\n*NONE\n\nText\n\nGOTHIC\n\n10 POINTS\n\nROMAN\n\nBOLD\n\nPress\n\nEnter\n\nto\n\ncontinue.\n\nF12=Cancel\n\nF3=Exit\n\nThis display shows the definition of a type 3 font.\n\nThe following table explains the Display Source Overlay Font display and the Display PFD Definition Font display\n\n<table>\n  <tr>\n    <th>Field Name</th>\n    <th>Description</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td>Font number Font type Code page Font character set Point size Text</td>\n    <td>Shows the font number: Shows the font type (Code page and font character set) Shows the code page name. Shows the font character set name Shows the size. Shows the description of the font. point</td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n\n# 9=Set Initial Font\n\nTo change the definition of a font to the initial values; do the following on the Work with Source Overlay Fonts display or the Work with PFD Definition Fonts display\n\n1 Type 9 in the Opt. column beside the font number for which you want to change the definition:\n\nPress Enter:\n\n",
